    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4340-287X"
abstract: >
  We introduce AutoTAB, an automated algorithm to track bipolar magnetic regions (BMRs)
  over their lifetime on the solar disk using MDI and HMI magnetograms from 1996 to 2020.
  AutoTAB successfully tracked 9,152 BMRs, enabling a detailed study of their evolution,
  tilt angles, flux, and statistical properties. This tool provides new insights into
  solar magnetic field evolution and activity cycles.
keywords:
